# SSO VietProDev Project Rules

## Core Security Rules

- NEVER log passwords, access tokens, refresh tokens, authorization codes, client secrets, or CSRF tokens.
- NEVER commit `.env` files, private keys, JWKS private keys, or real credentials.
- ALWAYS use timing-safe authentication: error messages for invalid user and invalid password must be identical.
- ALWAYS use `@nestjs/throttler` for rate limiting on login and token endpoints.
- ALWAYS use CSRF protection on login/logout/consent forms via `csurf` middleware.
- ALWAYS implement account lockout after N failed login attempts (configurable via env vars).

## Code Quality

- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run format` before every commit.
- All TypeScript must pass `npm run typecheck`.
- All new code must pass tests (`npm test`).
- Error handlers MUST sanitize sensitive data in responses (never leak tokens, codes, secrets).
- No `any` casts without comment explaining why it's necessary.
- Use `argon2` with `argon2id` type for password hashing.

## OIDC/SSO Rules

- PKCE must use `S256` method, never `plain`.
- Redirect URIs must be exact match, never wildcard.
- OIDC discovery endpoints should be used instead of hardcoded URLs (with fallback).
- All OIDC clients loaded from DB/config, never hardcoded.

## Database Rules

- Migrations must be idempotent: use `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` and `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS`.
- Migrations must be backward compatible: never drop columns in the same release that removes them from app code.
- All tables must have indexes on frequently queried columns (email, user_id, client_id, created_at).
- Audit write failures must be retried automatically (not silently swallowed).
- Production DB connections must go through PgBouncer/HAProxy, never directly to PostgreSQL nodes.

## Demo Project Rules

- Demo projects use `bindResource()` convention in `src/router.ts` (emulates `express-automatic-routes`).
- Demo project `sso.service.ts` stateStore must have TTL-based cleanup.
- All error handlers must sanitize OAuth error responses.
- Mark in-code comments when something is "demo-only" (e.g., in-memory stateStore).
